r_own":0.06864,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":45.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":["flagged"],"description_full":"The Kroger Co. operates as a food and drug retailer in the United States. The company operates combination food and drug stores, multi-department stores, marketplace stores, and price impact warehouses. Its combination food and drug stores offer natural food and organic sections, pharmacies, general merchandise, pet centers, fresh seafood, and organic produce; and its multi-department stores provide apparel, home fashion and furnishings, outdoor living, electronics, automotive products, and toys. The company's marketplace stores offer full-service grocery, pharmacy, health and beauty care, and perishable goods, as well as general merchandise, including apparel, home goods, and toys; and its price impact warehouse stores provide grocery, and health and beauty care items, as well as meat, dairy, baked goods, and fresh produce items. It also manufactures and processes food products for sale in its supermarkets and online; and sells fuel through its fuel centers. The company sells its products through its stores, fuel centers, and online platforms. The Kroger Co. was founded in 1883 and is based in Cincinnati, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Gregory S. Foran | CEO & Director | Age 64","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 400K people. Revenue per employee of $369K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers. Each employee generates $9K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $392 per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Kroger Company (The) is a large-cap consumer defensive business with a $41.8B market cap on $147.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 6% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $3.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 7.20\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 3.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 8.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 6.9% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $6.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Defensive peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 52% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 22% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","20 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 10% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"5 Disadvantages Of Grocery Shopping At Kroger","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/5-disadvantages-grocery-shopping-kroger-150300000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794591813.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.039,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"History of Kroger: Company timeline, facts & milestones","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/history-kroger-company-timeline-facts-142500000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794590902.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Digimarc Corp (DMRC) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Secure Gift Card Momentum Builds as ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/digimarc-corp-dmrc-q3-2026-010148158.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794618108.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"7 Things Animal Rescues Wish You\u2019d Donate More Often, According To Experts","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/7-things-animal-r