nst $15.9B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, and interest cover is thin at 3.0x.","The current ratio of 0.80 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 2.3% over 3 years, 2.2% over 5 years and 3.0% over 10 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 2% of profits supports about 0.2% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -2.6% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.2x, 2.6% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 4, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 2.7% on average."],"own":["Insiders own 6.9%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 85%.","It returns 8.1% a year to shareholders (6.0% in buybacks and 2.2% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 4.3% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 20 consecutive years, raising it 12.7% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 400,000 employees, each generates about $369K of revenue, 0.7x the Consumer Defensive median, and revenue has grown 4.2% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $9K of free cash flow per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":62,"head":"Invest: trades 52% below fair value of $147; Altman Z in the safe zone.","pros":["Composite 43, above the 39 line (gates 13/26)","Trades 52% below fair value of $147","Altman Z in the safe zone","EV/EBITDA 7.9x vs sector 10.2x","P/FCF 12.1x vs sector 16.1x"],"cons":["Interest coverage only 3.0x","Piotroski F-score 3/9","P/E 39.3x vs sector 18.3x"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":124.59,"vc":{"base":146.58,"base_src":"dcf","bear":103.58,"bull":212.7,"alt_median":44.15,"n_alt":3,"gap":2.3198,"dispersion":0.5514,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (55% dispersion)","DCF is 232% above the other models' median ($44.15)"]},"med":{"pe":18.2995,"ev_ebitda